  "mechanical_review_limits": "Actual 1:1 registration and current CAD/native checked. Recessed head sits0.30 mm below plate; unprovided cap swept geometry and printed material are not qualified.",
  "residual_risks": [
    "Hat socket nominal3.00/1.45/2.00/0.20 mm, but exact barrel tolerance, flat-blade acceptance, spring depth and forces unknown. Nominal hole clearance is not guaranteed contact compatibility.",
    "Exact seller TTC/Kailh variant controlled drawings are missing. Preserve seller selection and do not inherit tighter tolerances from a different manufacturer variant. V1 nominal0.85 mm pin projection with ring is not proven spring engagement.",
    "NPTH locator containment calculation assumes2.60\u00b10.08 mm finished diameter and\u00b10.05 mm position. These are explicitly bounded fabrication assumptions, not a measured supplier lot or slot tolerance.",
    "Conservative3.00x1.20 mm head is recessed0.30 below plate. Actual printed collar strength, clip/ring/joint fit, cap travel and torque/cycle/2N deflection remain unmeasured.",
    "M1.4x7.50 mm under-head candidate gives2.20 mm nominal receiver engagement/0.60 mm tip reserve; actual length/point/print tolerances unqualified. Old9 mm screw is obsolete; do not substitute8/9/10 mm without full recalc.",
    "Three same-net exposed-via locations remain: leftU1D5, rightU1D18, rightD27pad1. They may wick solder; isolated vias are tented, not all vias. Keep solder out of socket contacts.",
    "Exact protected battery/lead/current rating and populated controller stack need receipt inspection. Leave charge boost open and verify shorts/polarity/POWER/RESET before energizing.",
    "Printed strength, powered scanning, charge transitions, BLE/RF and lifetime require real assembly tests. First lot is product with explicit possible rework; no performance/reliability guarantee."
  ],
  "post_receipt_acceptance": [
    "CON-ARCH-004: actual switch/ring/socket seating and contact before full soldering; align and tack receptacles, cool/reinsert, complete joints without contact-cavity solder. Test replacement cycles and70-key scan.",
    "CON-ARCH-006: measure printed dimensions/clip and both split joints, screw engagement/tip reserve, cap full travel, torque/retention and2 N deflection.",
    "CON-ARCH-007: battery insulation/lead strain relief, controller stack, polarity/short/POWER/RESET continuity before applying power.",
    "REL-ARCH-001: controlled charge/power transition and final assembled BLE/RF acceptance; preserve existing physical acceptance thresholds."
  ],
